enchilada: a join no longer waits for ever on a scan whose end never came

After wifid made us leave KSASN (toggling Private Wi-Fi Address), its next ASSOCIATE was logged but no join ever began and Settings spun: ws_poll starts a join only once wn.scanning is clear, and a scan started right after the leave (the station vdev stopped under it) never got its SCAN_EVENT. A join that has waited 6 s now drops that scan; should the firmware still be scanning, VDEV_START is refused and the join fails cleanly, so wifid gets an answer.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_mss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_mss.c
@@ -5627,6 +5627,24 @@
 			}
 		}
 	}
+	/*
+	 * 0337: a join waits for the scan in flight, and a scan whose end the firmware never reports
+	 * (one started right after a leave, the station vdev stopped under it) left wn.scanning set:
+	 * every later join waited for ever and wifid's join spun in Settings. After 6 s the scan is
+	 * dropped; if the firmware still scans, VDEV_START is refused and the join fails cleanly.
+	 */
+	static unsigned join_wait;
+	if (ws_req.join && wn.scanning) {
+		if (join_wait == 0) {
+			join_wait = t ? t : 1;
+		} else if (t - join_wait > 6000) {
+			printf("SWEET WLAN: join waited %u ms for a scan that never ended: scan dropped\n", t - join_wait);
+			wn.scanning = false;
+			join_wait = 0;
+		}
+	} else {
+		join_wait = 0;
+	}
 	if (ws_req.join && !wn.scanning) {
 		if (ws.state != WS_IDLE) {
 			bool joining = ws.state != WS_UP;
